 "$comment": "AEP-0002 Annex A machine-usable mapping fixture for the pi table, verified against the published extension types in @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent@0.80.6 (the tarball ships the vendor docs at the same version; the fork @oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent@16.4.6 is expected-compatible but UNANCHORED — its union diverges, see the design record). Each entry pins mapEvent at the adapter default posture (capture metadata; deltas OFF); entries whose behavior forks under the AEP_PI_DELTAS opt-in carry deltas_expected. expected is {type, data, subject, step}. Identity and runtime wiring (ctx.sessionManager -> session with cwd/session-file redacted-gated; runs synthesized per AGENT LOOP — agent_start opens, agent_end closes on the last assistant message stopReason, a retried loop is a NEW run; toolCallId -> cause pairing; x.pi.* at debug severity) are receiver state, smoke-pinned in the reference repository. Deliberate nulls: message/tool stream updates at the default posture; non-user message starts; non-assistant message ends. The message boundary facts stay x.pi.message.* while the registry’s message.user.submitted / message.agent.replied are RESERVED (the sub-profile has not graduated) — the AG-UI/Cline refusal, applied at design review. NO attention.*/tool.denied claims: approval outcomes are not visible on the upstream bus (the fork’s typed tool_approval_requested/resolved pair is the named trigger).",
